# 11. AI AGENT ARCHITECTURE

Implement the agent as a controlled state machine, not as an unrestricted autonomous loop.

The processing pipeline must be:

1. Receive command.
2. Validate input.
3. Load relevant device state.
4. Interpret user intent.
5. Generate structured plan.
6. Validate plan against the tool registry.
7. Apply safety and permission policies.
8. Present the plan to the user.
9. Obtain required approval.
10. Execute approved actions.
11. Read device state again.
12. Evaluate expected postconditions.
13. Record verification evidence.
14. Recover from eligible failures.
15. Produce a truthful final report.
16. Persist the execution record.

Every phase must have explicit state transitions.

Prevent duplicate execution when the user refreshes the page or retries a network request.

Use unique command IDs and idempotency keys where appropriate.

An interrupted workflow must not automatically repeat previously completed physical actions.

On restart, load persisted execution records and determine whether a workflow can safely resume.

If the actual execution state cannot be determined, mark it as uncertain and require reconciliation.

Never infer success from the absence of an exception alone.

